# Project guidelines

## Language and style

- Write all documentation in plain English, with complete sentences.
- Keep each commit focused on a single change, and describe it in the imperative mood.
- Prefer short functions with explicit names over long functions with comments.

## Commands

- Run `npm test` before proposing any commit, and report every failure.
- Use `npm run build` to check that the bundle still compiles.
- Never run `git push` without an explicit request.

## Code conventions

- Use `const` by default, and `let` only when a value really changes.
- Handle errors where they happen; never hide them in an empty `catch` block.
- Keep configuration values in `config/defaults.json`, never hard-coded in the source.

## Reviews

- Explain the reason for a change, not only what it does.
- Mention any skipped test, and say why it was skipped.
